{"version":"0.12.29","prev_tag":"v0.12.28","target":"default","tag_prefix":"","area_scope":[],"commits":[{"sha":"d296b4805720d1024b53239a85d960fae097963f","title":"Resume conversations and Flows from durable Session records (#1296)","files":["Cargo.lock","README.md","STYLE.md","TESTING.md","docs/agent-api.md","docs/architecture-reference.md","docs/architecture.html","docs/architecture.md","docs/architecture/codebase.md","docs/architecture/data.md","docs/architecture/delivery.md","docs/architecture/execution.md","docs/architecture/homes.md","docs/architecture/planning.md","docs/authoring.md","docs/conducting.md","docs/config.md","docs/getting-started.md","docs/glossary.md","docs/index.md","docs/lf-reference.md","docs/lf.md","docs/security.md","docs/subscriptions.md","docs/troubleshooting.md","docs/waves.md","python/tests/test_lifecycle_scorecard.py","rust/loopflow/Cargo.toml","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/child.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/task/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/journal.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/metrics.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/registry.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/relocate.rs","rust/loopflow/src/durable.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/agent.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/init.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/loopflow.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/review-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/start-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/sync-conflicts.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/surfaces/headless.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/surfaces/human-present.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/loop-decide.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/research.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/split-wave.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/wave_operate.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/wave_review-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/wave_start-chapter.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/config.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/exec.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/execution.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/flow/saved_skill.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/flow_graph.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/flow_output.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/invocation.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/launch.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/process.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/prompt.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/transitions.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/worktrees.rs","rust/loopflow/src/exec.rs","rust/loopflow/src/harness/claude.rs","rust/loopflow/src/harness/claude_history.rs","rust/loopflow/src/harness/codex.rs","rust/loopflow/src/harness/codex_connection.rs","rust/loopflow/src/harness/codex_history.rs","rust/loopflow/src/harness/conformance_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/harness/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/harness/opencode.rs","rust/loopflow/src/harness/opencode_history.rs","rust/loopflow/src/harness/opencode_mapping.rs","rust/loopflow/src/harness/testdata/opencode_error_turn.ndjson","rust/loopflow/src/harness/testdata/opencode_normal_turn.ndjson","rust/loopflow/src/harness/testdata/opencode_reported_usage.ndjson","rust/loopflow/src/harness/testdata/opencode_tool_lifecycle.ndjson","rust/loopflow/src/harness/testdata/opencode_trace_manifest.json","rust/loopflow/src/journal/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/activity.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/ask.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/discord.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/doctor.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/exec.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/flow_inventory.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/install.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/install/published.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/ops/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/placement.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/replay.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/runs.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/runs_watch.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/session.rs"]}],"merged_prs":[{"number":1296,"title":"Resume conversations and Flows from durable Session records","body":"Conversation identity, command outcomes, and Flow progress were scattered across files and overlapping records, making recovery and history difficult to follow. This PR gives each a durable owner so conversations retain their identity across reconnects and Flows resume from captured progress.\n\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:start -->\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Task:** [Data model: one table per user object, Session as a child of Run · LOO-298](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-298/data-model-one-table-per-user-object-session-as-a-child-of-run)\n> **PR lifecycle:** Merging PR 1 completes the Task.\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:end -->\n\n## What changes\n\n- Replace the Run owner with three SQLite records: Exec for an actual `lf` process, AgentSession for a conversation, and FlowSession for a started Flow.\n- Use one driver for Task and taskless Flows. Skills and mechanical steps execute through ordinary commands; retries retain the conversation, and only the selected successful native completion advances the Flow. Loop passes remain positions within one FlowSession.\n- Separate client replacement from provider lifetime, allowing Codex clients to reconnect without restarting the live engine. Retain feedback, failed-turn evidence, and original usage attribution.\n- Add indexed Session, Exec, and saved-Flow discovery. Support permanent Session binding to Tasks, including completed Tasks, and preserve Desktop terminals and drafts through discovery and pane replacement.\n- Make Linear Project status own chapter planning and history. Projects supply the default Flow; rotation preserves started Tasks and retires only proven untouched backlog.\n\n## Limits\n\nThe cutover removes historical import and intermediate-schema compatibility. Finished history is not imported. Installed conversion still requires a consistent database/filesystem backup and rehearsal of current-state retention; configured provider, Desktop, and Linear acceptance remain open. These boundaries are recorded in the [cutover status](docs/architecture-reference.md#cutover-status).\n\n## Checks\n\nRecorded gate evidence includes passing Python and website suites, formatting, and all-target Clippy. Full Rust and Swift runs had failures subsequently addressed by focused repair checks; those repairs do not establish a clean full run of the final head. See the [retained gate evidence](wave/infrastructure/MEMORY.md#data-model-and-performance-decisions-reconciled-2026-09-30). No checks were rerun for this description.\n\n## Try it\n\nSuggested walkthrough, not performed for this description: use `lf session list` to select a conversation, rename it with `lf session rename SESSION \"Review notes\"`, then reconnect with `lf session connect SESSION`. The conversation should retain its identity and name; `lf session history SESSION --json` exposes its recorded history.","files":[],"additions":43237,"deletions":24821,"changed_files":320,"merge_commit":"d296b4805720d1024b53239a85d960fae097963f"}],"decisions":null,"previous_release_notes":"# v0.12.28\n\n<!-- loopflow:release-notes=narrative;gate=safe -->\n\nv0.12.28 makes finishing work more predictable: Task lifecycle commands coordinate issue, PR, checkout, and branch cleanup while preserving delivery history and reporting incomplete cleanup. Contributor verification also fits unattended runs, with focused checks during implementation and broader acceptance at gate. Upgrade for fewer manual cleanup steps and Desktop checks that run without a display session or permission dialogs.\n\n## Finish or cancel work with its cleanup attached\n\nTask outcomes now own the cleanup that previously required separate commands. Completion protects unmerged local work, cancellation closes retained unmerged PRs, and retries preserve effects that already succeeded.\n\n- Use `lf task abandon` with an issue ID, retained branch, or the current checkout to cancel the Linear issue and local Task, close retained unmerged PRs, and remove their checkouts and branches. Retries still work after the checkout disappears.\n- Completed delivery is cleaned after its worker stops and settles its claim. Cleanup preserves dirty files and branch tips beyond the merged head. Standalone PR landing also cleans up; bare Task landing retains the checkout for continued work.\n- `lf task delete` cancels unfinished placed work or cleans completed delivery before trashing the issue. Task, PR, and Run history remain readable.\n- Preview old-chapter cleanup with `lf task sweep --json`, including eligible open issues in archived Projects. `--apply` rechecks membership before cancellation. Worker claims, open PRs, unreconciled merges, dirty checkouts, and unavailable evidence prevent cancellation.\n- Live or unresolved workers block cancellation and deletion; pending cancellation prevents new worker claims. Cleanup failures report how to retry.\n\n## Verify changes without a display session\n\nVerification now belongs to the phase that can use its results. Implementation stays focused on changed code, while gate owns affected suites and automated acceptance; unavailable infrastructure routes checks to a capable environment without counting them as passed.\n\n- Implement and compress run changed-code builds and focused tests. Gate runs broader checks once and reuses applicable results. Actual build and test failures still require repair.\n- Default Desktop verification runs under WindowServer denial in gate and CI. It inspects production Work views in four states and invokes the real navigation button.\n- Window, Metal, PTY, and hosted UI checks become optional diagnostics. The default gate drops the duplicate Desktop build and window-capture step.\n- Headless inspection does not prove visual rendering or native integration correctness. Those remain part of opt-in diagnostics and demo/review.\n\n## Operational notes\n\n- **Command migration:** replace `lf wt remove` and `lf wt rm` with `lf wt delete`. The shared deletion operation removes remote branches too. Lower-level PR and worktree operations retain the Task outcome.\n- **Operate by issue:** `lf task pr ISSUE ACTION` and `lf task sync ISSUE` address delivery operations through the Task's issue.\n- **Validation:** lifecycle proofs used simulated provider responses with real disposable Git repositories and remotes; configured abandonment and sweep acceptance remain pending after installation. The later verification change records passing Python, Rust, headless Swift, architecture, multiplatform boundary, Xcode compilation, and lint checks. CI owns the remaining matrix.\n\n## Small changes\n\n- A per-skill check-time and context collector adds a dated baseline. Runtime savings remain unmeasured pending comparison with later Runs.\n- Scratch check summaries are kept to one line to reduce repeated verification context.","source_limits":{"context_bytes":131072,"commits":256,"merged_prs":200,"files_per_change":100,"area_scopes":32,"name_bytes":256,"title_bytes":300,"path_bytes":512,"pr_body_bytes":4096,"decisions_bytes":16384,"previous_release_notes_bytes":16384,"release_notes_bytes":61440},"omissions":{"commits":0,"merged_prs":0,"commit_files":228,"pr_files":0,"area_scopes":0,"text_bytes":0,"decisions_bytes":0,"previous_release_notes_bytes":0}}